WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.790
Since making his debut as the Dark Knight
in 2016's Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice,

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.430
Ben Affleck's name has become as synonymous
with Batman as Jared Leto's has with the Joker,

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.090
Margot Robbie's has with Harley Quinn, and
Gal Gadot's has with Wonder Woman.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:18.890
Affectionately referred to as "Batfleck" by
fans of his contributions to the DC Extended

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.150
Universe, Affleck puffed out his chest, mustered
up his courage, and assumed the mantle once

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.180
occupied by screen icons Adam West, Michael
Keaton, Val Kilmer, George Clooney, and the

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.240
unforgettable Christian Bale, who lead Christopher
Nolan's Dark Knight trilogy.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.880
Now, Affleck is hanging up his cape and cowl
and handing the suit over to someone new - someone

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.410
who could be Robert Pattinson.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.120
Yes, rumor has it that Warner Bros. is eyeing
the Twilight Saga alum to become the next

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:47.680
Batman, making his first appearance in director
Matt Reeves' The Batman, the long-gestating

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.120
film that Affleck was initially supposed to
lead.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.579
Since appearing in Twilight, Pattinson has
established himself as a legit actor with

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:57.320
acclaimed roles in the films High Life and
Good Time.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.969
And the internet has noticed, taking such
a liking to the idea of Pattinson as Batman

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:06.060
that digital artists have started creating
artwork imagining what the British star would

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.300
look like all done up as the Caped Crusader.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.640
Using a Batman concept suit designed by 3D
generalist and CG artist Christophe Lacaux,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.200
Twitter user @NovaMCU shared their creation
on the site on February 11.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.420
Pattinson is just one of many names allegedly
in the running for the role of Batman.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.840
Revenge of the Fans editor-in-chief Mario
Robles claimed on an episode of his The Fanboy

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.249
YouTube series that Pattison was up against
the likes of Kick-Ass star Aaron Taylor-Johnson,

00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:36.579
Lone Ranger lead Armie Hammer, and Game of
Thrones stars Richard Madden and Kit Harington,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.700
among many others.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.560
But it's Pattinson that seems to have really
captured people's imaginations, with popular

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.500
BossLogic wrote,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.859
"A choice that I never would have thought
to try [I've] but been hearing some background

00:01:45.859 --> 00:01:50.149
chatter about Robert Pattinson being looked
at, if the [source is] true then all of our

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:51.360
predictions were wrong.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.940
This might be your new Bruce"

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:57.719
It goes without saying that this is all hearsay,
grapevine gossip, unconfirmed chit-chat floating

00:01:57.719 --> 00:01:58.719
around the internet.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:02:03.190
Warner Bros. hasn't confirmed or denied reports
of Pattinson becoming the next Batman, and

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.029
director Reeves hasn't made so much as a peep
about who the next Batman might be.

00:02:07.029 --> 00:02:11.260
The studio is apparently looking for someone
younger than Affleck to portray Batman next,

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.420
with The Batman said to center around a young
version of the famous DC Comics hero.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:21.080
Pattinson is only 32 to Affleck's 46 - and
that 14-year age gap falls almost perfectly

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:25.220
in line with past reports that claimed Warner
Bros. wants the newest iteration of Batman

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.610
to be 15 to 20 years younger than Affleck,
and the character to be between 25 and 30

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.810
years old in the movie.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.110
If Warner Bros. decides to go older, though,
Pattinson might face some serious competition

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.250
from a couple of established superstars, namely
Jake Gyllenhaal and Jon Hamm.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.920
Gyllenhaal has been a top contender for the
role of Batman in the past, and though in

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.180
2018 he denied he would be the next Batman,
things can change pretty fast in Hollywood.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.960
And as for Hamm, he's reportedly been campaigning
for the role for a long time.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.800
Back in December, 2017, RadarOnline cited
a source that claimed

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.341
"Jon knows Ben has faced some criticism over
Batman v Superman and Justice League, and

00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:02.950
frankly thinks he'd be better suited for the
job.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.920
This is business for Jon — not personal.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.690
[…] The writing's on the wall, and Jon's
desperate for the gig."

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:12.540
Since Gyllenhaal is 38 and Hamm is 47, it
seems unlikely that either of the two men

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.940
will end up leading The Batman.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.920
But who knows?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.440
After Christian Bale left the role, nobody
was expecting Ben Affleck to take it over,

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.660
so now that Affleck is leaving, who knows
what Warner Bros. will decide.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.960
It could even be some other name nobody was
expecting to hear.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.440
"Martha!"

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:35.740
Either way, the studio has scheduled The Batman
to soar into theaters on June 25th, 2021,

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.770
so fans should expect an announcement soon
about which actor will play the part - whether

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:41.240
it's Pattinson or not.

